Modifications: save-systems became references/save-systems.md and the
timestep half of physics-tuning became the loop section; both were rewritten
in the house style with engine API removed. From GodotPrompter, the
engine-neutral state-machine choice (enum, per-state objects, hierarchical,
parallel, data-driven; the upgrade triggers; "name the rejected approach"),
the inventory decisions and the ability, effect, stat-modifier and tag model
were condensed into references/patterns.md, with GDScript and C# code
replaced by pseudocode. Fixes applied on port: nested state machines enter
and handle input only while their parent is active; the inventory registry
is built from an explicit list rather than a directory scan (which fails in
exported builds), and items are saved by id, never by resource path;
ability cast time is enforced through a casting state; effects are keyed by
effect id and source with an explicit stacking policy instead of by
definition object; gameplay tags are counted. From save-load, the rule that
engine-native resource files must never be used for user-writable saves was
kept in engine-neutral form. Added: JSON number pitfalls, pool generation
handles, event-bus rules and a save test checklist.

